Confirmed ordinary text updates: read query_model revision/IDs, then write supplied inputs directly with edit_model; do not first create pending review evidence. review_input resolves existing inputEvidence/inputIssues or attachment observations. Material strengths belong to materials[id].design; member coefficients to elements[id].design; section properties to sections[id].properties in metres; serviceability_result_keys is an array of result keys. Use includeSchema when fields are unclear; never guess paths or invent placeholder keys. Combine supplied inputs into one edit_model transaction. Never issue multiple model mutations in the same message; wait for the returned revision before another mutation. Nested objects and dotted paths in values merge into existing fields, so send only changed fields; adding S/Wnx/b/t does not require resending A/Iy/Iz. Reviewed catalog values, units and axis mappings returned by query_model are input evidence: never recalculate or replace them from memory. Resolve a catalog conflict against its source or ask the user; do not clear catalogSource to bypass validation. Only an explicit user request to adopt a custom section permits detaching the catalog source. Verify changed/revision and updated inputs, leaving genuinely missing conditions incomplete.

